# Taiwan 3D (`טייוואן 3D`) — Persistent Project Context

Interactive 3D travel web app for a 33-day trip to Taiwan (`6.11 – 8.12.2026`), built with Next.js 16 (App Router, strict TypeScript), Three.js r186, `@react-three/fiber`, `@react-three/drei`, Zod, Framer Motion, and Tailwind CSS v4.

## Directory & Modular Architecture Map

Keep all files small (**target < 250 lines, hard cap < 390 lines**) and organized by feature domain:

- `/data`: Pre-built static JSON (`cities.json` [19 cities], `route.json` [10 legs, 33 days], `attractions.json` [147], `food.json` [80], `hotels.json` [37], `overrides.json`, `practical.json`, `images/credits.json`), `types.ts`, and `build.py`. **Never re-parse Excel in runtime code.**
- `/lib/data`:
  - `schemas.ts`: Strict Zod schemas derived from `data/types.ts`. Fails build if any `cityId` is invalid.
  - `coordinates.ts` & `taiwanGeo.ts`: Projects `[lat, lng]` to 3D island space (`latLngToXZ`, `latLngToWorld3D`), computes Central Mountain Range DEM elevation (`getElevationAtLatLng`), and calculates deterministic golden-angle spiral offsets (`resolvePlaceCoordinates`).
  - `loaders.ts` & `selectors.ts`: Validated static dataset (`TRIP_DATA`), selectors by city/leg/day/place, `buildGoogleMapsUrl`, and `formatDisplayPriceText`.
  - `search.ts`, `foodAndPlaceMeta.ts`, `placeImages.ts`, `imageMatchers.ts`, `cityTransitGuides.ts`: Modular helpers for search, food/hotel metadata, Haversine distance, Taiwan UTC+8 open-hours check, and Wikimedia Commons image resolution.
- `/lib/store`:
  - `tripStoreTypes.ts` & `useTripStore.ts`: Hydration-safe `useSyncExternalStore` + `localStorage` store for display and map session only (`isNightMode`, `selectedCityId`, `focusedPlaceId`, `sheetSnap`, `currentDayIndex`, `layerToggles`). This is an info app: do not add favorites, visited/done tracking, hotel picks, or a personal budget.
- `/components/3d`:
  - `MapCanvas.tsx` & `MiniTaiwanMap.tsx`: R3F `<Canvas>` wrappers with `<WorldHtmlHost />`.
  - `CameraRig.tsx` + `/components/3d/camera/` (`cameraMath.ts`, `useCameraPointerAndKeys.ts`): Fit-to-island camera pose, half-sheet reframing, pointer pan, double-tap zoom, and keyboard controls.
  - `TaiwanIsland.tsx`, `OceanWater.tsx` + `/components/3d/island/` (`polygonMath.ts`, `terrainBuilder.ts`, `oceanBuilder.ts`): Extruded coastline, offshore islands, DEM mountain shader, and SDF coastline water shader.
  - `CityPins.tsx` + `/components/3d/pins/SingleCityPin.tsx`: 3D city pins, label nudges, Kenting dashed marker, and offshore island labels.
  - `CategoryMarkers.tsx` + `/components/3d/markers/` (`markerConfig.ts`, `InstancedCategoryGroup.tsx`, `MarkerTooltipCard.tsx`): GPU-instanced category markers with `>=44px` hit spheres and zoom LOD.
  - `CityDestination3DMap.tsx` + `/components/3d/city-map/` (`cityMapLayout.ts`, `DestinationPinModels.tsx`, `SingleDestinationPin.tsx`, `CityDestination3DScene.tsx`, `CityDestinationHUD.tsx`, `FocusedDestinationCard.tsx`): Zoomed-in 3D city diorama and HUD.
  - `DelightDetails.tsx` + `/components/3d/delight/LandmarkDioramas.tsx`: Mini Taipei 101, Sun Moon Lake cable car, Alishan train, sky lanterns, and clouds.
  - `WorldHtml.tsx` + `/components/3d/overlay/labelOverlapSolver.ts`: React 19 DOM overlay host and 2D overlap solver.
  - `Map2DFallback.tsx`, `TaiwanLoadingScreen.tsx`, `threeCompat.ts`. Do not add a route tube, driving car, or timeline play button.
- `/components/ui`:
  - `Navbar.tsx`, `LayerToggles.tsx`, `TimelineScrubber.tsx`, `BottomSheet.tsx`, `PlaceCard.tsx`, `PlaceDetailClient.tsx`, `CommandSearch.tsx`, `MapNavigationPad.tsx`, `PwaRegister.tsx`.
  - Feature subfolders: `/components/ui/drawer/` (`CityDrawerTabsContent.tsx`), `/components/ui/food/` (`FoodFilterSheet.tsx`), `/components/ui/route/` (`RouteLegCard.tsx`), `/components/ui/info/` (`EmergencyAndPhrasesSection.tsx`, `ImageCreditsDetails.tsx`).
- `/app`: `/` (3D map home), `/route` (10 legs synced with sticky 3D mini-map), `/food` (80 spots + sticky filter bar), `/hotels` (37 hotels with best cheap pick first), `/info` (practical guide, Mandarin audio phrasebook, emergency dialers), `/place/[id]` (SSG for all 264 places).

## Non-Negotiable Data, Code & UI Rules

1. **Small Files & Single Responsibility**: Keep components and modules focused and under **300–390 lines**. Extract subcomponents, hooks, geometry builders, and pure utilities into feature subfolders (`/components/3d/<feature>/`, `/components/ui/<feature>/`, `/lib/data/`) rather than growing monolithic files.
2. **No Hardcoded IDs**: Place IDs (`attr-xxx`, `food-xxx`, `hotel-xxx`) depend on Excel row order. Never hardcode place IDs in components.
3. **Route Truth**: `route.json -> legs` (10 legs, 33 days) is the source of truth. `route.json -> audit` is historical archive only.
4. **Price & Verification Display**:
   - Always display `priceText` (via `formatDisplayPriceText`) for hotels and food; use `priceMin`/`priceMax` only for sorting and budget math.
   - Any unverified price or hours (`!verified`, `!priceVerified`, `!hoursVerified`) must show a `"לא מאומת"` badge.
5. **RTL & Hebrew**: Keep all Hebrew strings untouched (`dir="rtl"`, `lang="he"`, Rubik/Heebo fonts).
6. **No Orange Route Line on Map**: Do not render a 3D tube or 2D polyline connecting the route path on the island map.
